From aea09525db15e8f2edfb02e82830dd26f8937613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zahary Karadjov <zaharyk@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:02:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Never reap a runner the forge reports busy

A pool runner that is executing a job can be reported "offline" by
GitHub while it is still busy: its listener session lapses when the
host is starved or briefly partitioned, but the job carries on. The
runner cleanup loop does not read the busy flag at all.

- reapTimedOutRunners() times a runner out from the instance's
  UpdatedAt, which is not refreshed while a job runs, so every job that
  outlives runner_bootstrap_timeout is exposed. An offline-but-busy
  runner is handed to DeleteRunner(), and the forge's own 422 ("still
  running a job") is the only thing standing between it and the job.
  The refusal is then returned as an error, which ends the pass:
  the remaining instances are not looked at and runnerCleanup() skips
  cleanupOrphanedRunners() for the entity, on every pass, until the
  job ends.
- cleanupOrphanedProviderRunners() marks pending_delete, with no age
  check and without asking the forge, any instance whose name is
  missing from one listing of the forge's runners. The paginated list
  can drop a runner that moves between pages mid-listing, so a busy
  runner can lose its instance under a running job.
- cleanupOrphanedGithubRunners() treats an offline-but-busy runner as
  an orphan candidate; the forge refuses the removal and the error
  fails the whole sweep.

This change carries the forge's busy flag in forgeRunner (both the
REST listing and the scale set API report it) and:

- reapTimedOutRunners() skips a runner the forge reports busy, and
  keeps going when one DeleteRunner() fails, reporting all failures at
  the end;
- runnerCleanup() runs the orphan sweep even when the reap reported
  errors;
- cleanupOrphanedProviderRunners() retires an ACTIVE instance that is
  missing from the listing through DeleteRunner(), so the forge is
  asked first (422 while busy, "not found" when really gone);
- cleanupOrphanedGithubRunners() skips offline-but-busy runners.

runner/pool/busy_runner_reap_test.go drives runnerCleanup() and
cleanupOrphanedProviderRunners() against the real SQLite store with a
mocked forge client. Three tests reproduce the defects and fail without
this change; two controls (an idle timed-out runner is still reaped, an
active runner the forge no longer has is still retired) pass with and
without it.

Signed-off-by: Zahary Karadjov <zaharyk@gmail.com>
